  <h2 id="gcroutesb">A check before you act</h2>

  <p>
    Follow the ten percent rule of household income for education and aim for a caution limit of twenty percent. Example figures are an illustration, not a real fee.
  </p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="paths-table paths-table--wide">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Check</th>
          <th>Question</th>
          <th>Tip</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Check"><strong>Fit</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Question">Do I enjoy the daily work?</td>
          <td data-label="Tip">Spend a week observing or doing it</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Check"><strong>Cost</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Question">What will training cost in total?</td>
          <td data-label="Tip">Compare free and paid options</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Check"><strong>Entry</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Question">What do entry roles ask for?</td>
          <td data-label="Tip">Read five notices</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Check"><strong>Growth</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Question">What does year three look like?</td>
          <td data-label="Tip">Ask two people in the field</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 id="gcroutesc">A twelve-week plan</h2>

  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="paths-table paths-table--wide">
      <thead>
