          <td data-label="Output">Requirements table</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Weeks"><strong>3 to 5</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Task">Spend time observing or helping in the field and keep notes</td>
          <td data-label="Output">Field notes</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Weeks"><strong>6 to 9</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Task">Design, simulate and document a small digital circuit, such as a counter or a simple adder, using free tools.</td>
          <td data-label="Output">Project or sample</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Weeks"><strong>10 to 12</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Task">Talk to three people in the field and write a decision note</td>
          <td data-label="Output">Decision note</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 id="vlflow">From idea to chip: the stages in plain words</h2>

  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="paths-table paths-table--wide">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Stage</th>
          <th>What happens</th>
          <th>Typical role</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Stage"><strong>Specification</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What happens">Decide what the chip must do</td>
          <td data-label="Typical role">Architect</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Stage"><strong>RTL design</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What happens">Describe the logic in a hardware language</td>
          <td data-label="Typical role">Design engineer</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Stage"><strong>Verification</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What happens">Test the design against many cases</td>
          <td data-label="Typical role">Verification engineer</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Stage"><strong>Synthesis and layout</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What happens">Turn logic into physical shapes and check timing</td>
          <td data-label="Typical role">Physical design engineer</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Stage"><strong>Fabrication</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What happens">Manufacture the chip in a plant</td>
          <td data-label="Typical role">Process engineer</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Stage"><strong>Test and validation</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What happens">Check the real chip works</td>
          <td data-label="Typical role">Test or validation engineer</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    Seeing the whole chain helps you pick the stage that fits your temperament.
  </p>
  <p>
    Ask someone in the field which stage they would choose again.
  </p>

